ngs call the race Likely or Solid Democratic; markets price about 95% for Democrats", "Recent polls show narrowing, including an R-sponsored survey at just +2 and a headline noting Demuth rising", "Open seat in a D+3 state, with a $10 million outside infusion boosting Demuth"], "rationale": "Klobuchar combines deep name recognition and a dominant money advantage in a Democratic-leaning state, and every expert rating and prediction market treats her as a clear favorite. Polls still show a high-single-digit lead even after visible late tightening toward Demuth, so a Likely Democratic rating with a margin near nine points fits the evidence.", "watch": "The October 21 debate and whether Demuth's $10 million outside infusion keeps narrowing the polls could move this race.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Tim Walz (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Minnesota's governorship is open with Tim Walz retiring, and Democrats have turned to Senator Amy Klobuchar while House Republican leader Lisa Demuth carries the GOP banner. Klobuchar holds large advantages in name recognition and money, raising about $7 million to Demuth's $360,000, though a Demuth-affiliated committee received a $10 million infusion and the contest is already the most expensive in state history.\n\nPolls since mid-September show Klobuchar ahead by two to ten points, a narrower spread than summer surveys, and outside raters uniformly call the race Likely or Solid Democratic. Prediction markets price Democratic chances around 93 to 95 percent. The state has leaned Democratic by about three points in recent cycles, and the main remaining events are an October 21 debate and the effect of heavy outside spending on the late trend.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9683, "margin": 10.03}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9647, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.931, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9507, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_d